    "id": "v2-543ca-p31-practice-slot-13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Use trigonometry to find the length of the projection of $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ onto $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ if $|\\overrightarrow{OA}|=4\\sqrt6$ and $\\angle AOB=135^\\circ$.\n\nHint: draw a diagram.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4\\sqrt3$",
      "worked": "Let $H$ be the perpendicular foot from $A$ to the line $OB$. Since $\\angle AOB$ is obtuse, $H$ lies on the extension of $BO$ beyond $O$, and $\\angle AOH=180^\\circ-135^\\circ=45^\\circ$. The length of the projection is $OH$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\cos45^\\circ&=\\frac{OH}{4\\sqrt6}\\\\OH&=4\\sqrt6\\cos45^\\circ\\\\OH&=4\\sqrt6\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right)\\\\OH&=2\\sqrt{12}\\\\OH&=4\\sqrt3\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
